NEARS-1475 — QA live probe, Widgetbook release web build (Chrome/Playwright, light mode)
Story: components/nmoduleswitcher/nmoduleswitcher/playground

CLAIM UNDER TEST: the anchored overlay inherits an ANCESTOR-injected MediaQuery /
Directionality. It does not — it opens as a route on the ROOT navigator.

--- text scale: in-story text scales, overlay rows do not ---
text-scale={factor:1.0}
  app-bar location node "Tower 4, Al Reem":  x=357 y=12 w=706 h=36
  overlay rows: 55 / 55 / 49 / 48
text-scale={factor:1.3}
  overlay rows: 55 / 55 / 49 / 48          <-- unchanged
text-scale={factor:2.0}
  app-bar location node "Tower 4, Al Reem":  x=357 y=2  w=706 h=56   <-- addon DOES apply
  overlay rows: 55 / 55 / 49 / 48          <-- unchanged

--- RTL: trigger + anchoring mirror, row internals do not ---
locale={name:ar-SA}
  trigger      x 305.2 -> 1090.8            (mirrored, 16px inset from logical start)
  menu.right   1134.8 == trigger.right      (anchored to the logical near edge)
  barrier      "Dismiss menu" -> "إغلاق القائمة"   (captured at the call site)
  screenshot   ac4-rtl-arabic-overlay-open.png: row leading disc still LEFT,
               check / NEW tag still RIGHT  <-- row internals not mirrored

MECHANISM: showMenu captures the layout textDirection and the barrier label at the
CALL SITE (so those mirror), but the item widgets are inflated inside the route, whose
ancestors are the root navigator's Localizations / MediaQuery. In the real UserApp the
app-level Localizations sits above the navigator, so this is expected to be a storybook
artifact — but it means BOTH of the following are unproven, not proven:
  * the overlay's 1.3x text-scale behaviour (unit test
    'renders at 1.3x text scale without overflow' injects MediaQuery inside
    MaterialApp.home, i.e. the same ancestry shape the overlay escapes);
  * the overlay row's RTL internal mirroring.
